-- ============================================================================
-- Migration 84: notebook_schema.rejected_extensions — a curator's "no" that
-- survives the next document (Track PC.5).
--
-- `reject_extension` dropped the pending row and recorded nothing, so the next
-- document proposing the same type put it straight back in the queue. PC.1
-- pinned that with two tests, one per layer, so the gap could not pass for a
-- guarantee; this closes it.
--
-- Same shape and semantics as `excluded_types` (migration 46), which already
-- makes a soft-DELETE survive a re-proposal: `merge_pending_extensions` skips
-- any name in either list, case-insensitively on the trimmed name.
-- `option<array<string>>` because rows written before this migration read the
-- field as NONE; the model coerces NONE to [].
--
-- Staging held one notebook_schema row (79 pending, 0 accepted) when this was
-- written, and no drift on the table's fields.
-- ============================================================================

DEFINE FIELD IF NOT EXISTS rejected_extensions ON TABLE notebook_schema TYPE option<array<string>>;
